  14. A test fails when two calls of one stage, whose shared opening the provider in use could reuse, declare different answer formats.
       requirements: completion-02
       code evidence: not required — The requirement itself demands a test failure case, so the obligation is satisfied by the test alone.
       test evidence: unsupported  [tier: static]
         (no mapped test)
         recommended test: A test case showing two reusable-prefix calls from one stage with different answer formats fails.
           inputs:  Use one mapping-stage batch with at least two candidate tests in the same call, and make the fake model return two entries for the same `test_id` but with different answer shapes across the duplicate entries (for example, first entry has a non-empty `obligation_ids` list and second entry has an empty list or a differently shaped rationale). The key is that both entries target the same batch item so the defect changes whether the second answer is silently ignored or explicitly recorded.
           detects: A repeated `test_id` from one stage is silently deduplicated or absorbed, so inconsistent duplicate answers do not surface as an unusable answer and the tool quietly chooses one answer without recording that a conflict occurred.
           full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion test-fails-on-inconsistent-answer-formats

